{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPass 3 (`src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py`: `validity()`, `impact_plan()`, `pass3_decide`, `pass3_over_findings`, `DEFAULT_BLOCK_THRESHOLD`, per-criterion `block_threshold`/`default_posture` in `criteria_routing.json`) is deterministic and every input it needs — the Pass-2 `verification` vector, `block_threshold`, `blocking_enabled`, `review_phase` — is in the v2 sidecar. `docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py` and `docs/experiments/calibrate_plan_review_thresholds.py` prove the replay works but are one-off scripts with hardcoded baselines. Any proposal touching Pass-3 logic or thresholds should be assessable over the corpus for free.\n\n`review_kernel.decide.pass3_over_findings(findings, verifs, *, threshold_for, impact_fn=None, execution_review=False)` is the OVERLAY-CAPABLE kernel entrypoint: `threshold_for` resolves a candidate's per-criterion thresholds/postures, `impact_fn` is a caller-supplied candidate impact model. `orchestrator.pass3_over_findings` hardcodes both from live config and cannot take an overlay.\n\n`corpus.build_corpus`'s cache rows (`cache_dir / f\"{content_hash}.jsonl\"`) are SUMMARY rows only (`store, ticket_id, review_event_ts, review_event_uuid, verdict, material_fingerprint, ...`) — they carry NO per-finding `findings`/`verification`/`block_threshold` data. Getting that requires the SAME re-read pattern `labels.py` already uses: `corpus._enumerate_event_blobs(tracker_path)` + `corpus._batch_cat` to fetch the FULL `REVIEW_RESULT` blob `data` for a cache row's `review_event_uuid` (matched by uuid), then read `data[\"findings\"]` (each carrying `verification`/`criteria`) — `pass3_over_findings`'s `verifs` argument is the `{index: verification}` map built from that same `findings` list's order.\n\n`docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py` solves the plan-v4→plan-v5 cross-version replay: pre-v5 sidecars carry ORDINAL grades (`low|medium|high`) that plan-v5's `impact_plan` kind model rejects directly. Its `classify(axis, text)` (regex `RULES`, gap-biased) maps each graded row's finding body to its nearest plan-v5 KIND before `rescore(attrs, kinds)` feeds `decide._PLAN_GRADE_MAPS`. Tier-0 reuses this mapping, not a fictional direct feed.\n\nTicket-level labels (`labels.py`, closed) need a `show_ticket` call per ticket — too slow at full-corpus scale (committed evidence: a real 40-ticket subset). Tier-0's Pass-3 replay needs NONE of that (all inputs come from the re-read sidecar `data`), so label-proxy metrics are SEPARATE, OPTIONAL: computed only over whatever committed `labels-<hash>.jsonl` is supplied, with the report stating the coverage fraction.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier0.py` (+ `report.py`, `__main__.py`):\n\n- Input: the corpus (`corpus.build_corpus`), an OPTIONAL `labels_path` (read via `labels.load_labels`; absent/mismatched-hash omits label-proxy metrics, never a hard failure), and a **candidate** = `impact_fn` + a routing-overlay JSON building `threshold_for` + `[verify]` overrides. Default candidate = live `criteria_routing.json` + `impact_plan` (identity check).\n- **Full-body re-read (fixes the missing-findings gap)**: for each corpus cache row, re-read its `REVIEW_RESULT` blob's full `data` via `corpus._enumerate_event_blobs` + `corpus._batch_cat` matched by `review_event_uuid` — the SAME pattern `labels.py`'s `_findings_for_row` already uses. `data[\"findings\"]` is the `findings` list `pass3_over_findings` takes; `verifs = {i: f.get(\"verification\") for i, f in enumerate(findings)}` is its `verifs` map.\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__main__.py`: `python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier0 --candidate <name>` subcommand dispatch (also wires `ledger.print_summary()` per the ledger ticket's note).\n- Run `review_kernel.decide.pass3_over_findings(findings, verifs, threshold_for=..., impact_fn=...)` for baseline and candidate over every corpus review's re-read findings; keep the stored per-finding decision (already in `data[\"findings\"]`, e.g. `decision`/`reason`) as the historical reference. Pure computation over re-read sidecar data — no `show_ticket` — so this is the part the 5-minute timing AC applies to.\n- Plan-v4→v5 replay (AC2): for pre-v5 sidecars, apply `plan_v5_rescore.classify`/`RULES` to map each graded axis to its plan-v5 kind BEFORE `impact_plan`, reusing that script's mapping (import it, or port `RULES`/`classify` verbatim if not importable as a package module).\n- Report (`tier0-<candidate-name>-<date>.md` + JSON): verdict flip matrix (PASS/BLOCK/INDETERMINATE), friction rate, per-criterion block/advisory/drop deltas, priority distribution shift. IF `labels_path` supplied: label-proxy metrics with explicit coverage fraction, annotated against the labels ticket's noise band. ELSE states label-proxy metrics were not computed.\n- Post-verdict floors (novelty/completion/drift) replayed only when their inputs are present in the sidecar; otherwise reported as not replayed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier0.py` (new) — full-body re-read + Pass-3 replay\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/report.py` (new) — diff report rendering\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__main__.py` (new) — module entry point / subcommand dispatch\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/tier0-*.md` (generated)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier0.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: identity replay of a fixture corpus (re-reading `findings`/`verification` from a real git tracker fixture, same TrackerBuilder pattern as `labels.py`/`corpus.py`, feeding `pass3_over_findings` with `threshold_for`/`impact_fn` matching the fixture's stored decision) yields zero diffs; a candidate overlay lowering one criterion's threshold flips exactly the fixture findings whose priority sits between old and new thresholds; a v1 sidecar lacking `block_threshold` is skipped and counted; a pre-v5 graded row is classified to a plan-v5 kind via the reused mapping before rescoring; label-proxy metrics are omitted (not crashed) when no `labels_path` is supplied; `__main__.py`'s `tier0` subcommand dispatches to `tier0.run(...)`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier0 --candidate current` over the real corpus reports zero verdict flips against stored decisions for reviews whose `impact_model_version` matches current; checked by the generated report.\n- [ ] Replaying the plan-v4→plan-v5 change (via the reused `plan_v5_rescore` grade→kind mapping) reproduces its documented direction and approximate magnitude; checked against `docs/calibration/`.\n- [ ] The report contains verdict flip matrix, friction rate, and per-criterion deltas from the pure Pass-3 replay; checked by inspection of one report.\n- [ ] IF a labels file is supplied, the report additionally contains label-proxy recall/false-positive metrics with their coverage fraction, annotated relative to the noise band; checked by inspection when a labels file is available.\n- [ ] The Pass-3 replay itself (excluding any optional label-proxy step) completes in under 5 minutes on a laptop over the real corpus, with zero LLM calls; checked by timing and by running without provider credentials.\n- [ ] Unit tests pass in `make test`."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788084280425111676,"uuid":"dc73459c-6efd-4243-b056-70380f2415e7"}